; meter-odd: the tick grid off the common path — 7/8 meter at the
; fractional tempo 128.5. PPC = 720720 divides 7 and 8 exactly, so
; every beat stays an exact integer tick even here; the fractional bpm
; moves only the seconds↔ticks seam (one mul+floor). `arc` runs a full
; in-out-cubic rise and an out-expo fall across the two-bar loop — b
; and bar position units mix freely. `mark`'s second key is authored in
; SECONDS (3 s = 6.425 beats — off the BEAT grid, reached through the
; documented seam) and still lands bit-exactly on its authored f32 (structural
; landing: the eval-time 3.0 s clock converts through the SAME mul+
; floor and selects the key's own segment edge). `lfo` is the classic
; unipolar cosine off `phase`, sweeping 0→1→0 once per 7-beat bar.
; :emit [bar phase] rides the odd grid. 128.5 bpm: 1 beat ≈ 0.46693 s,
; 1 bar (7 beats) ≈ 3.26848 s, the 2bar loop ≈ 6.53696 s.
(transport :bpm 128.5 :meter [7 8] :dur 2bar :end loop :emit [bar phase])

(track :target arc
  (key :at 0b :value 0.0)
  (key :at 1bar :value 1.0 :ease in-out-cubic)
  (key :at 2bar :value 0.0 :ease out-expo))

(track :target mark
  (key :at 0b :value 0.2)
  (key :at 3s :value 0.8))

(track :target lfo :expr (* 0.5 (- 1 (cos (* (tau) phase)))))
